1
00:00:01,162 --> 00:00:04,575
ditto-chaos: chaos engineering for an Eclipse Ditto digital-twin sandbox.

2
00:00:04,675 --> 00:00:08,113
Before the test, the target is healthy: no errors, no lost updates.

3
00:00:08,213 --> 00:00:11,639
100 synthetic twins in three product categories, all fresh and valid.

4
00:00:11,739 --> 00:00:17,272
Nine services are running, and the healthy baseline is valid.

5
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:21,974
The operator switches to manual mode to choose the fault.

6
00:00:22,074 --> 00:00:25,370
Fault: freeze the search service (pause on things-search), 12 seconds at most.

7
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:30,671
Preview first: a policy check that executes nothing.

8
00:00:30,771 --> 00:00:34,953
It lists the exact commands, the rollback order and the stop conditions.

9
00:00:35,053 --> 00:00:41,932
A real fault needs explicit operator authorization.

10
00:00:42,032 --> 00:00:45,505
The controller checks policy, containers and current health before touching anything.

11
00:00:45,605 --> 00:00:50,667
The Pipeline tab follows the run stage by stage. Stage 4, Baseline: health is confirmed first.

13
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:59,622
Fault injected: the search service is frozen. The Monitor stage counts failed checks toward the kill switch.

14
00:00:59,722 --> 00:01:05,814
Live monitoring shows the same fault on the charts, as it happens.

15
00:01:05,914 --> 00:01:09,400
Kill switch: search endpoint failed on all of the last 3 ticks. Rolling back automatically.

16
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:12,600
Rollback verified. Measuring how long Ditto takes to recover.

16
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:17,557
Ditto recovered 2.0 seconds after the rollback.

17
00:01:17,657 --> 00:01:23,297
The charts show the impact: search failures during the fault, then back to normal.

18
00:01:23,397 --> 00:01:30,846
Back on the Pipeline: Monitor was stopped by the kill switch, and the rollback is verified.

19
00:01:30,946 --> 00:01:39,646
The agents lane shows what each of the seven agents concluded for this run.

20
00:01:39,746 --> 00:01:45,674
The report: stopped by the kill switch, rollback verified, recovered in 2.0 s.

21
00:01:45,774 --> 00:01:51,838
Impact is reported per product category, from measured data only.

22
00:01:51,938 --> 00:02:00,411
Findings: measured facts are labelled separately from hypotheses.

23
00:02:00,511 --> 00:02:09,541
Recommended fixes are proposed for an operator to decide. Nothing is applied automatically.

24
00:02:09,641 --> 00:02:19,843
Every run adds to the evidence base and re-ranks which experiment to run next.

25
00:02:19,943 --> 00:02:27,412
Injected, observed, stopped, verified, explained.
